<title>USA: TWA says to cut 1,000 jobs as new jets reduce needs.</title>
<headline>TWA says to cut 1,000 jobs as new jets reduce needs.</headline>
<dateline>ST. LOUIS, Mo. 1997-07-22</dateline>
<text>
<p>Trans World Airlines Inc. said Tuesday it will cut 1,000 jobs by December as it adds younger jets to its fleet, reducing maintenance needs.</p>
<p>The airline said the positions being eliminated include 250 posts at its overhaul base in Kansas City, Mo., and 625 in maintenance, airport operations and reservations.</p>
